.TH CLAUDE\-KEEPALIVE 1 "2026-09" "claude-keepalive" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-keepalive \- run claude and auto-resume after a usage-limit reset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-keepalive
.RB [ \-\-resume
.IR SESSION_ID ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs
.B claude
under a pseudo-terminal, watches its output for a usage limit, and resumes
the session automatically once the stated reset time has passed \(em rather
than leaving a long task stopped until someone notices.
.PP
Signals and terminal size changes are forwarded to the child, so it behaves
like running the command directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " SESSION_ID"
Resume an existing Claude session by id.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the wrapped command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start a session that survives a limit reset:
.PP
.RS
.B claude-keepalive
.RE
.PP
Resume a known session:
.PP
.RS
.B claude-keepalive \-\-resume 01H8Z...
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/claude-keepalive
.UE
